---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    A sim session is the hour you spend on a simulated frequency rather than
    reading about one. Twelve of them, one a week, and you transmit in the
    first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each page says what to bring, what happens in the order it happens, and
    what leaves the room. The <strong>spec</strong> on each one is a contract:
    if you cannot do those things afterwards, the session did not work, and
    saying so is more useful to us than attendance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Several sessions measure something about you — your confusion pairs in week
    2, your hearback miss count in week 3, your comprehension scores in week 9.
    None of those numbers is marked or appears in any assessment. They are
    deliberately free, because a measurement you are graded on is a
    measurement you will manage rather than take.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
